---
// Capabilities — light sand canvas.
// Grid of 8 capability cards, honest one-sentence descriptions, no invented stats.
---

<section id="capabilities" class="section">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="cap__header stack" data-animate>
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">What Luna handles</p>
      <h2 class="cap__heading">
        Built for the full front-desk conversation.
      </h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Luna isn't a FAQ bot. It handles the back-and-forth that turns
        an enquiry into a confirmed booking — and keeps your team informed
        at every step.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="cap__grid" role="list" data-animate>

      <li class="cap__card">
        <div class="cap__card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="cap__card-title">Availability &amp; service questions</h3>
        <p class="cap__card-text">
          Answers "what's free on Saturday morning?" with real slot data, not
          a guess — and follows up if the preferred time is taken.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="cap__card">
        <div class="cap__card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2L2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5zM2 17l10 5 10-5M2 12l10 5 10-5"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="cap__card-title">Packages &amp; pricing rules</h3>
        <p class="cap__card-text">
          Quotes accurately from your configured pricing rules — group rates,
          multi-day discounts, seasonal prices — without rounding, inventing,
          or hedging.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="cap__card">
        <div class="cap__card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 11l3 3L22 4"/><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="cap__card-title">Booking assistance</h3>
        <p class="cap__card-text">
          Collects names, dates, group size, and contact details in natural
          conversation, then surfaces a clean summary so a staff member can
          confirm in seconds.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="cap__card">
        <div class="cap__card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11 4H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-7"/><path d="M18.5 2.5a2.121 2.121 0 0 1 3 3L12 15l-4 1 1-4 9.5-9.5z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="cap__card-title">Changes &amp; add-ons</h3>
        <p class="cap__card-text">
          Handles reschedule requests, extra participants, and optional
          add-ons — checking real availability first, never confirming
          something it can't see space for.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="cap__card">
        <div class="cap__card-icon cap__card-icon--seaglass" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="cap__card-title">Staff handoff</h3>
        <p class="cap__card-text">
          Knows when to stop and involve a person — discretionary decisions,
          complaints, or anything outside its scope — and flags it clearly
          in the shared inbox.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="cap__card">
        <div class="cap__card-icon cap__card-icon--seaglass" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="cap__card-title">Shared inbox &amp; context</h3>
        <p class="cap__card-text">
          Every conversation is visible to the whole team with full history.
          Staff stepping in see exactly what was said, not a forwarded
          screenshot chain.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="cap__card">
        <div class="cap__card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 8v4l3 3"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="cap__card-title">Business-specific tone &amp; rules</h3>
        <p class="cap__card-text">
          Luna learns your voice — formal or casual, surf-school friendly or
          boutique precise — and respects your specific policies without
          needing to be reminded each time.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="cap__card">
        <div class="cap__card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M2 12h20M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="cap__card-title">Multi-language</h3>
        <p class="cap__card-text">
          Luna detects the language the guest writes in and continues
          the conversation in that language — Spanish, English, French,
          German, and more — without switching unless the guest does.
        </p>
      </li>

    </ul>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cap__header { max-width: 680px; }
  .cap__heading { font-size: var(--step-4); margin-top: var(--space-xs); }

  .cap__grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-m);
  }
  @media (min-width: 560px) {
    .cap__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .cap__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
  }

  .cap__card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    padding: var(--space-m) var(--space-m) var(--space-l);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-s);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    transition: box-shadow var(--dur) var(--ease-out), transform var(--dur) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .cap__card:hover {
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-m);
    transform: translateY(-3px);
  }

  .cap__card-icon {
    width: 2.4rem;
    height: 2.4rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
    background: var(--sand-100);
    color: var(--terracotta-600);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .cap__card-icon--seaglass {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--seaglass-500) 12%, transparent);
    color: var(--seaglass-600);
  }

  .cap__card-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }

  .cap__card-text {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    flex: 1;
  }
</style>
